{"base_rate":0.17333333333333334,"brier":0.10281850000000001,"bss":0.28243912841191054,"bss_hi":0.4693320248164005,"bss_lo":0.060926879801027956,"chart":{"base":[286.8,62.0],"fp":[194.2,233.8],"lead":"62,240.1 272,227.7 482,220.6 692,201.7","note":{"base":"skill 0.28 — higher than 50% of cities","fp":"low end -0pp, high end +31pp","lead":"day-1 error 1.2 °C — better than 37% of cities","rel":"promised 0% → rained 0%; promised 91% → rained 59%"},"rel":"62.1,466 263.5,348.8 637.7,211"},"country":"TD","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.07801666666666665,"ess":287.7255068913006,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for N&#x27;Djamena</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The N&#x27;Djamena rain forecast is moderately skilful, though 2 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (98%), believe about\n<b>69%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>0%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 600 days, 2024-05-10 to\n2026-03-25. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nthe station, 3.2 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.28, ranked 106 of\n213 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(31&ndash;179) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>0%</b></td><td class='num'>360</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>14%</td><td class='num'><b>15%</b></td><td class='num'>59</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>50%</td><td class='num'><b>39%</b></td><td class='num'>59</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>84%</td><td class='num'><b>48%</b></td><td class='num'>58</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>98%</td><td class='num'><b>69%</b></td><td class='num'>64</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">2 of 5 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>N&#x27;Djamena</b> <span class=\"muted\">Chad</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag ok\">Moderately skilful</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">2 points off by more than chance</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>0.28</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>31&ndash;179\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 213</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>600 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    N&#x27;Djamena &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for N&#x27;Djamena\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"58.03933333333333,380.9888888888889 107.38,301.79661016949154 235.12,153.72881355932205 354.0172413793103,49.37931034482756 406.35812500000003,18.0 406.35812500000003,35.0625 354.0172413793103,112.13793103448273 235.12,246.27118644067795 107.38,357.3220338983051 58.03933333333333,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"318.90666666666664\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"318.90666666666664\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"58.03933333333333,382.0 107.38,326.47457627118644 235.12,240.10169491525423 354.0172413793103,206.27586206896552 406.35812500000003,131.75\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 0% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 360 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"58.03933333333333\" cy=\"382.0\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 14%&amp;#10;It rained 15% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 59 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"107.38\" cy=\"326.47457627118644\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 50%&amp;#10;It rained 39% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 59 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"235.12\" cy=\"240.10169491525423\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 84%&amp;#10;It rained 48% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 58 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"354.0172413793103\" cy=\"206.27586206896552\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 98%&amp;#10;It rained 69% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 64 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"406.35812500000003\" cy=\"131.75\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(17%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In N&#x27;Djamena the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>autumn</b> (0.30) and least in\n<b>summer</b> (-0.15).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>142</td><td class='num'>48%</td><td class='num'>-0.150</td><td class='num'>21.8%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>117</td><td class='num'>3%</td><td class='num'>0.248</td><td class='num'>1.1%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>167</td><td class='num'>19%</td><td class='num'>0.304</td><td class='num'>9.4%</td></tr><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>174</td><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'>nan</td><td class='num'>0.0%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":12.10672,"lon":15.0444,"n":600,"n_cities":213,"name":"N'Djamena","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.014000000000000342,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.00011111111111111112,"n":360,"obs":0.0,"sig":false},{"hi":0.31,"lo":0.014000000000000342,"mean":0.13949152542372878,"n":59,"obs":0.15254237288135594,"sig":false},{"hi":0.71,"lo":0.31,"mean":0.5003389830508475,"n":59,"obs":0.3898305084745763,"sig":false},{"hi":0.94,"lo":0.71,"mean":0.836206896551724,"n":58,"obs":0.4827586206896552,"sig":true},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.94,"mean":0.9840625000000001,"n":64,"obs":0.6875,"sig":true}],"prcp_km":3.2,"provisional":false,"rank":106,"rank_hi":179.02499999999998,"rank_lo":30.975,"reliability":0.02267502459399419,"resolution":0.060132596272485225,"skill_pct":null,"slug":"ndjamena","station":"","timezone":"Africa/Ndjamena"}